# The project root has collected a number of zero-byte files from mistyped
# shell redirects, so the root is a whitelist: ignore everything, then add back
# only the real project entries. Anything new at the root must be listed here
# on purpose, which also stops a stray .env.serverN from ever being committed.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/ecosystem.config.js
!/.env.example
!/src/
!/tests/
!/scripts/
!/data/

# Runtime state and dependencies.
node_modules/
data/*
!data/capes.json

# Secrets. Each PM2 instance has its own .env.serverN on the host; none of them
# and no .env ever belong in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!/.env.example
